.bd B 3
.TH hex2000 1 "May 20, 2026" "TI Tools" "TI Code Generation Tools"
.SH NAME
hex2000 - Hex Converter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hex2000
[
.I options
] [
.I file(s)
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The hex converter converts an object file into one of several standard hexadecimal formats.
.SH OPTIONS
The following options are accepted by this tool:
.SS General Options:
.SS
.TP
-byte
Output as bytes rather than target addressing
.TP
--cmac=file
Specify CMAC key file name and enable CMAC signature generation
.TP
-e=addr
Specify entrypoint address or symbol name
.TP
-exclude=section
Exclude section from hex conversion
.TP
-fill=val
Specify fill value
.TP
-h
Display a help message that includes usage and option information [Same as -options]
.TP
-image
Select image mode
.TP
-linkerfill
Include linker fill sections in images
.TP
-map=file
Specify map file name
.TP
-memwidth=width
Specify memory width
.TP
-o=file
Specify output file names
.TP
-options
Display a help message that includes usage and option information [Same as -h]
.TP
-order=LS,MS
Specify data ordering (endianness)
.TP
-q
Quiet Operation [Same as -quiet]
.TP
-quiet
Quiet Operation [Same as -q]
.TP
-romwidth=width
Specify rom width
.TP
--sb
Swap output bytes for 16byte memwidth
.TP
-z
Zero based addressing [Same as -zero]
.TP
-zero
Zero based addressing [Same as -z]
.SS Diagnostics Options:
.SS
.TP
--diag_error=id
Treat diagnostic <id> as error
.TP
--diag_remark=id
Treat diagnostic <id> as remark
.TP
--diag_suppress=id
Suppress diagnostic <id>
.TP
--diag_warning=id
Treat diagnostic <id> as warning
.TP
--diag_wrap[=on,off]
Set diagnostic messages to wrap at 79 columns (on) or not (off). The argument to the option is optional, and if not specified it will default to: on
.TP
--display_error_number
Emit diagnostic identifier numbers
.TP
--issue_remarks
Issue remarks
.TP
--no_warnings
Suppress warnings
.TP
-pdb
Line buffer diagnostic output to reduce message mixing when compiling in parallel.
.TP
-pdew
Treat warnings as errors
.TP
--set_error_limit=count
Set error limit to <count>
.SS Boot Table Options:
.SS
.TP
-boot
Select boot mode
.TP
-bootorg=addr
Specify origin address or symbol of boot table ROM
.TP
--boot_align_sect
Align boot table split blocks to section alignment
.TP
--boot_block_size=size
Set block size for splitting of boot table records
.TP
-can8
Specify table source as the GP I/O port, 8-bit mode [Same as -gpio8]
.TP
-divsel=value
Specify the initial value for the DIVSEL register. Valid only if -xintf8/xintf16 is used
.TP
-gpio16
Specify table source as the GP I/O port, 16-bit mode
.TP
-gpio8
Specify table source as the GP I/O port, 8-bit mode [Same as -can8]
.TP
-i2c8
Specify I2C port as source of boot table loader
.TP
-i2cclkh=value
Specify the initial value for I2CCLKH register
.TP
-i2cclkl=value
Specify the initial value for the I2CCLKL register
.TP
-i2cpsc=value
Specify the initial value for I2CPSC register
.TP
-lospcp=value
Specify the initial value for the LOSPCP register
.TP
-pllcr=value
Specify the initial value for the PLLCR register. Valid only if -xintf8/xintf16 is used
.TP
-sci8
Specify table source as the SCI-A port, 8-bit mode
.TP
-spi8
Specify table source as the SPI-A port, 8-bit mode
.TP
-spibrr=value
Specify the initial value for the SPIBRR register
.TP
-xintcnf2=value
Specify the initial value for the XINTCNF2 register. Valid only if -xintf8/xintf16 is used
.TP
-xintf16
Specify parallel XINTF stream, 16-bit mode
.TP
-xintf8
Specify parallel XINTF stream, 8-bit mode
.TP
-xtiming=value
Specify the initial value for the XTIMING register. Valid only if -xintf8/xintf16 is used
.SS Output Format Options:
.SS
.TP
-a
Output ASCII hex format
.TP
--array
Array output format
.TP
-b
Binary output format (for DSKs)
.TP
-i
Output Intel hex format
.TP
-m[=1,2,3]
Output Motorola S hex format
.TP
-t
Output TI-Tagged hex format
.TP
--ti_txt
Output TI-TXT hex format
.TP
-x
Output Extended Tektronix hex format
.SS Load Image Options:
.SS
.TP
--host_image
Deprecated. Use --load_image --load_image:combine_sections=false --load_image:output_symbols=true --load_image:section_prefix=<machine> instead
.TP
--host_image:endianness=big,little
Deprecated. Use --load_image:endian instead.
.TP
--host_image:hidden_symbols
Deprecated. Use --load_image:symbol_binding=local instead
.TP
--host_image:hide=string
Deprecated. Use --load_image:localize instead.
.TP
--host_image:show=string
Deprecated. Use --load_image:globalize instead.
.TP
--host_image:target=ARM,MSP430,C2000,C6000,PRU
Deprecated. Use --load_image:machine instead
.TP
--load_image
Output a load image object file. A load image contains all sections which are required to be loaded onto the target. All sections are converted to data and all debug information is removed. The output format can be controlled using the various --load_image: options.
.TP
--load_image:combine_sections=true,false
If this option is set to true, sections will be combined if the gap between their start and end addresses is less than the machine word size. The default section names will be image_<index>.
.TP
--load_image:endian=big,little
Specify the object file endianness
.TP
--load_image:file_type=relocatable,executable
Specify the output file type
.TP
--load_image:format=coff,elf
Specify the object file format
.TP
--load_image:globalize=string
Explicitly make a load image symbol visible. Overrides the default binding chosen with --load_image:symbol_binding=local.
.TP
--load_image:localize=string
Explicitly make a load image symbol hidden. Overrides the default binding chosen with --load_image:symbol_binding.
.TP
--load_image:machine=ARM,MSP430,C2000,C6000,PRU,C7X
Specify the object file machine name
.TP
--load_image:output_symbols=true,false
Specify if symbols should be output to the file.
.TP
--load_image:section_addresses=true,false
If the output file type is relocatable, this option can be used to include the section's load address in the sh_addr field. This field is typically not used by linkers and the TI linker will discard it, but the information could be useful for a custom ELF processing tool.
.TP
--load_image:section_prefix=string
Specify the prefix for the section names. The prefix will be appended to each section name separated by a ':'. The special argument <machine> will prefix the section names with the input machine name, ARM:.text for instance.
.TP
--load_image:symbol_binding=local,global
Determine the binding for symbols in the resulting load image. If set to local, all global symbols will have local binding in the load image file. Use --load_image:localize and --load_image:globalize to change the binding of individual symbols. The default behavior is global.
.TP
--section_name_prefix=string
Deprecated. Use --load_image:section_prefix instead.
.SS Additional Array Format Options:
.SS
.TP
--array:name_prefix=string
Prefix for array names in array output format. Arrays will be named PREFIX_0, PREFIX_1, etc..
.SH EXIT STATUS
The following error values are returned:
.PD 0
.TP 10
.B 0
Successful completion.
.TP
.B >0
Unsuccessful completion; an error occured.
.PD
